00:16:42.000 --> 00:17:33.000
out of the office. Many of us work from home these days, especially since the pandemic, and we have our work emails on our personal phones and computers so we can check any time. Has workaholism gotten more common, do you think, as technology has made us more reachable? What we do know from the research is that technology does tether us to work in an unhealthy way. And simply just having that access to work 24-7 and them having access to you 24-7, really what it's hindering is your ability to psychologically detach from work. because you're always, you know that you're always possibly reachable. And having that technology is very tempting. If you have these workaholic tendencies,

25
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:51.000
you're much more likely to have your email go to your phone and check it just throughout the day. Just it almost becomes a habit. A lot of us have this, you know, just if we're bored, if we're in line at the grocery store, what do we do? We pull out our phone and maybe check our email. Maybe you can relate to that.

